From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhishek Sahu <abhsahu@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 11:53:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: platform/arm64: nvidia-ffa-ec: add OEM and
 standard FFA service UUIDs

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167300

ACPI tables collected from GB10 platforms issue FFA
requests through the FFAC channel for service UUIDs not yet listed in
nvidia_ffa_ec_service_ids[]. Without a matching entry the FFA bus
framework does not create a per-service device for those partitions,
so the FFH handler cannot route the AML packet to the correct FFA
endpoint and the AML method aborts.

Add the standard ACPI Physical Presence service UUID
(3dddfaa6-361b-4eb4-a424-8d10089d1653, defined as
UUID_PHYSICAL_PRESENCE in include/acpi/acuuid.h) and seven OEM-specific
service UUIDs observed across GB10 platforms. The OEM entries cover
platform-defined services such as vendor management, EC RAM access,
WMI BIOS attributes, SMBIOS extensions, and other custom services.

The OEM entries are grouped under a single "custom UUIDs used by OEM
platforms" comment because their FF-A service definitions are
platform-defined and not published in a public spec. The Physical
Presence entry is a standard ACPI service and is called out separately.

Signed-off-by: Abhishek Sahu <abhsahu@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
Ledger-Change: C-02132
Ledger-Origin: nvidia-bos@36b661759a603d6d03e2c8899f7420c8080c67b1
---
 drivers/platform/arm64/nvidia-ffa-ec.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/arm64/nvidia-ffa-ec.c b/drivers/platform/arm64/nvidia-ffa-ec.c
index 8a7639b24098..7975a90d38f3 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/arm64/nvidia-ffa-ec.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/arm64/nvidia-ffa-ec.c
@@ -967,6 +967,26 @@ static const struct ffa_device_id nvidia_ffa_ec_service_ids[] = {
 	/* time/alarm */
 	{ UUID_INIT(0x23ea63ed, 0xb593, 0x46ea,
 		    0xb0, 0x27, 0x89, 0x24, 0xdf, 0x88, 0xe9, 0x2f) },
+
+	/* Physical Presence (UUID_PHYSICAL_PRESENCE, include/acpi/acuuid.h) */
+	{ UUID_INIT(0x3dddfaa6, 0x361b, 0x4eb4,
+		    0xa4, 0x24, 0x8d, 0x10, 0x08, 0x9d, 0x16, 0x53) },
+
+	/* Custom UUIDs used by OEM platforms. */
+	{ UUID_INIT(0xa3e7f7cf, 0x66ca, 0x43b9,
+		    0x9b, 0x6e, 0x99, 0x47, 0xb8, 0xe2, 0xa5, 0x11) },
+	{ UUID_INIT(0x884a63a0, 0x3285, 0x4120,
+		    0x83, 0xaa, 0xee, 0xc0, 0x08, 0xa0, 0xa5, 0x46) },
+	{ UUID_INIT(0x378daedc, 0xf06b, 0x4446,
+		    0x83, 0x14, 0x40, 0xab, 0x93, 0x3c, 0x87, 0xa3) },
+	{ UUID_INIT(0x3592e053, 0xe409, 0x4ce0,
+		    0xa0, 0x89, 0x97, 0xbd, 0x53, 0x37, 0x1c, 0x88) },
+	{ UUID_INIT(0x8a61cc5c, 0x2bbb, 0x4e29,
+		    0xa0, 0x2e, 0x02, 0x17, 0xe3, 0xf2, 0x42, 0x5a) },
+	{ UUID_INIT(0xde5dca60, 0x9fec, 0x47fb,
+		    0x85, 0x68, 0xdf, 0xf1, 0xf5, 0x42, 0x13, 0x83) },
+	{ UUID_INIT(0x73cc07ac, 0xd184, 0x4b5a,
+		    0x89, 0x07, 0x83, 0x7c, 0x5b, 0x0a, 0xe1, 0x2b) },
 	{}
 };
 
